{"abstract":"The evolution of Digital Musical Instruments (DMIs) has pushed the boundaries of musical expression and interaction. These instruments leverage advanced technologies to offer new dimensions of creative possibilities. This paper investigates the musical possibilities of Bodyharp [1] and the Teinophon [2], each designed to go beyond the limits of traditional instruments. We aim to uncover new perspectives on performer interaction and mapping, using the capabilities of these instruments to surpass traditional stringed-instrument boundaries with their infusion of sensor-based technologies. The study focuses on crafting and analyzing inventive mappings that connect the performer's gestures to sound, extending digital musical interactions beyond traditional instrument techniques dictated by physical and acoustical limitations. We explore uncharted sonic territories, drawing inspiration from the instruments' familiarities, yet extending them to create unique musical interactions. Through qualitative and performance-based examination of the interaction between body movements and sonic outcomes, we identify mappings that offer the most compelling and engaging results. This research recognizes the personal nature of musical preferences while encouraging creative exploration following a workshop-style evaluation method. We collected data from eight participants based on their experience with exploring both instruments' affordances and with solo and collaborative performance practices. Our work contributes to the broader discussion on sensor-based instruments, providing insights into their potential for expanding musical expression beyond established norms. By sparking further innovation and exploration, we hope to deepen our understanding of the creative possibilities embedded in Bodyharp and Teinophon, thus paving the way for new dimensions in contemporary musical expression.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fogadić, Leo","Cavdir, Doga Buse","Overholt, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805563"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-06","place":"Porto, pt","start":"2024-07-04","title":"21st Sound and Music Computing Conference, SMC 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring uncharted soundscapes innovative interaction and mapping techniques with the bodyharp and the teinophon","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14337378","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-805563","identifier":[{"id":"105000299375","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dd00061b-9f33-4e86-981d-c785179be22a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D93F3C74FEAC62A6D080D543F85C4EB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.14337378","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/778005331/SMC2024_paper_id190.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Multisensory Experience Laboratory","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leo","key":"fogadićleopau","last":"Fogadić","locid":"a07f762b-6175-4ea5-8d8f-674079b89ddd","name":"Fogadić, Leo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Doga Buse","key":"cavdirdogabusepau","last":"Cavdir","locid":"9573a42f-77a3-470d-a611-a7d773830354","name":"Cavdir, Doga Buse","orcid":"0000-0003-0169-2945","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dan","key":"overholtdanielpau","last":"Overholt","locid":"ffec9cea-8641-4c7f-b9e4-9f57c427bda8","name":"Overholt, Daniel","name_org":"Overholt, Dan","orcid":"0000-0003-2127-2868","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guilherme","key":"camposguilhermepedh","last":"Campos","name":"Campos, Guilherme","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ines","key":"salselasinespedh","last":"Salselas","name":"Salselas, Ines","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jose","key":"vieirajosepedh","last":"Vieira","name":"Vieira, Jose","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"conceicaomarcopedh","last":"Conceicao","name":"Conceicao, Marco","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nuno","key":"fonsecanunopedh","last":"Fonseca","name":"Fonseca, Nuno","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rui","key":"penharuipedh","last":"Penha","name":"Penha, Rui","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Angela da","key":"ponteangeladapedh","last":"Ponte","name":"Ponte, Angela da","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dimitrios","key":"andrikopoulosdimitriospedh","last":"Andrikopoulos","name":"Andrikopoulos, Dimitrios","rank":17,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.14337378","eisbn":["9789893520758"],"issn":["25183672"],"pages":"191-196","publisher":"Sound and Music Computing Network","series":"Proceedings of the Sound and Music Computing Conference","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 21st Sound and Music Computing Conference, SMC 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dd00061b-9f33-4e86-981d-c785179be22a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Exploring Uncharted Soundscapes : Innovative Interaction and Mapping Techniques with the Bodyharp and the Teinophon","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805563","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introducing GestoLumina (GeLu), a novel interface by the Universal Music Design (UMD) team at CymaSpace, whose mission is to enhance arts and culture accessibility for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (DHH). UMD is a program that applies principals taken from the ”Universal Design” concept towards music accessibility and inclusion for the DHH. The primary goal of UMD is to create experiential, educational pathways for the DHH to interact with music in a meaningful way. GeLu is the first UMD interface in the framework and is modular in its feature set allowing the user to choose, based on use case, between visual and/or haptic feedback along with gestural sensing. GeLu combines two bracelets: a ring system with gesture sensing and haptic feedback; and an audio-reactive LED color feedback array. The ring system captures tactile input through sensors and provides haptic feedback on the fingertips. The audio-reactive LED color feedback bracelet visualizes audio data, creating dynamic visualizations synchronized with sound.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hergert, Nate","Simeone, Dillon","Cavdir, Doga Buse","Macconnell, Duncan","Trail, Shawn","de Bastion, Myles"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794560"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-06","place":"Utrecht, nl","start":"2024-09-02","title":"International Conference on New Interfaces for Musical Expression, NIME 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Avid Technology, Inc.","Confluence Recording Company","CymaSpace"],"keyword":["Haptic","Inclusion","Interface"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gestolumina gesture interpreted light sound and haptics towards a framework for universal music design","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13904794","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-794560","identifier":[{"id":"85207654068","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-620d298c-5183-4cba-8177-f46693ee648f"],"keyword":["Deaf/DHH","audio-visualization","haptic","inclusion","interface"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-00776C342994F8A76635D39511B7E481"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.13904794","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/771515943/nime2024_15.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"confluence recording company","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Confluence Recording Company","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"avid technology inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Avid Technology, Inc.","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"cymaspace","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"CymaSpace","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nate","key":"hergertpau","last":"Hergert","name":"Hergert, Nate","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dillon","key":"simeonepau","last":"Simeone","name":"Simeone, Dillon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Doga","key":"cavdirpau","last":"Cavdir","locid":"9573a42f-77a3-470d-a611-a7d773830354","name":"Cavdir, Doga Buse","name_org":"Cavdir, Doga","orcid":"0000-0003-0169-2945","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Duncan","key":"macconnellpau","last":"Macconnell","name":"Macconnell, Duncan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shawn","key":"trailpau","last":"Trail","name":"Trail, Shawn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Myles","key":"debastionpau","last":"de Bastion","name":"de Bastion, Myles","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5281/zenodo.13904794","issn":["22204792"],"journal":"Proceedings of the International Conference on New Interfaces for Musical Expression","pages":"100-103","publisher":"International Conference on New Interfaces for Musical Expression","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on New Interfaces for Musical Expression"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85207654068"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-620d298c-5183-4cba-8177-f46693ee648f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"GestoLumina : Gesture interpreted Light, Sound and Haptics. Towards a Framework for Universal Music Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794560","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This article presents design and performance practices for movement-based digital musical instruments. We develop the notion of borrowed gestures, which is a gesture-first approach that composes a gestural vocabulary of nonmusical body movements combined with nuanced instrumental gestures. These practices explore new affordances for physical interaction by transferring the expressive qualities and communicative aspects of body movements; these body movements and their qualities are borrowed from nonmusical domains. By merging musical and nonmusical domains through movement interaction, borrowed gestures offer shared performance spaces and cross-disciplinary practices. Our approach centers on use of the body and the design with body movement when developing digital musical instruments. The performer’s body becomes an intermediate medium, physically connecting and uniting the performer and the instrument. This approach creates new ways of conceptualizing and designing movement-based musical interaction: (1) offering a design framework that transforms a broader range of expressive gestures (including nonmusical gestures) into sonic and musical interactions, and (2) creating a new dynamic between performer and instrument that reframes nonmusical gestures—such as dance movements or sign language gestures—into musical contexts. We aesthetically evaluate our design framework and performance practices based on three case studies: Bodyharp, Armtop, and Felt Sound. As part of this evaluation, we also present a set of design principles as a way of thinking about designing movement-based digital musical instruments.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cavdir, Doga Buse","Wang, Ge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726051"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"borrowed gestures the body as an extension of the musical instrument","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85148059857&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-726051","identifier":[{"id":"85148059857","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-97fcdb21-97ef-43df-b570-6a2e7e85ee86"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CF1DE737CBDCA99644AEE80990EFD833"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Doga","key":"cavdirpau","last":"Cavdir","locid":"9573a42f-77a3-470d-a611-a7d773830354","name":"Cavdir, Doga Buse","name_org":"Cavdir, Doga","orcid":"0000-0003-0169-2945","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ge","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1162/comj_a_00617","issn":["01489267","15315169"],"issn_org":["01489267"],"issue":"3","journal":"Computer Music Journal","pages":"58-80","publisher":"MIT Press Journals","status":"p","title":"Computer Music Journal","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-97fcdb21-97ef-43df-b570-6a2e7e85ee86"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Borrowed Gestures : The Body as an Extension of the Musical Instrument","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726051","year":"2021","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Mutualizing the body and the instrument offers a different way of thinking about designing embodied musical interfaces. This research presents the design of the BodyHarp, a wearable instrument that combines large bodybased gestures with the fine control of hand-based instruments. This reflects a desire to create a single interface that both captures expressive, dance-like, body movement as well as nuanced gestural interactions. The BodyHarp was not designed as a separate artifact, but rather it was crafted as an augmentation to the human body. This fusion seeks to enhance the sense of intimacy between the player and the instrument and carries a different type of aesthetic - like playing a traditional instrument (the harp) but as part of the body. In other words, the BodyHarp aims to capture creative body movement and placing it in an instrumental context. In doing so, we aim to blur the transition between two gestural mediums (dance and playing an instrument) by mutualizing them - or, in a sense, by designing the interface as a part of the body.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cavdir, Doga Buse","Michon, Romain","Wang, Ge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-725788"],"event":{"end":"2018-07-07","place":"Limassol, cy","start":"2018-07-04","title":"15th Sound and Music Computing Conference, SMC 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the bodyharp designing the intersection between the instrument and the body","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85075103670&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-725788","identifier":[{"id":"85075103670","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-62e75174-5681-42e1-bec8-2837c49e554a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0639F0DAF9EAEEC5277A012953A59857"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Doga Buse","key":"cavdirpau","last":"Cavdir","locid":"9573a42f-77a3-470d-a611-a7d773830354","name":"Cavdir, Doga Buse","orcid":"0000-0003-0169-2945","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Romain","key":"michonpau","last":"Michon","name":"Michon, Romain","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ge","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Ge","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anastasia","key":"georgakipedh","last":"Georgaki","name":"Georgaki, Anastasia","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Areti","key":"andreopouloupedh","last":"Andreopoulou","name":"Andreopoulou, Areti","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789963697304"],"pages":"498-503","publisher":"Sound and Music Computing Network","series":"Proceedings of the 15th Sound and Music Computing Conference: Sonic Crossings, SMC","status":"p","subtitle":"Sonic Crossings, SMC 2018","title":"Proceedings of the 15th Sound and Music Computing Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-62e75174-5681-42e1-bec8-2837c49e554a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The BodyHarp : Designing the intersection between the instrument and the body","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-725788","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
